  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "Final rules are strict on incident reporting (24h/48h), impose a 5% hard cap on 55°C testing with per-model results to customers/regulators but not public, require new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit, require built-in suppression after 36 months, and mandate recall above 8/100k with prompt notice. Both companies' red lines are satisfied, but each flagship model is banned by the strict S2 or S5 thresholds."
